AB  - We conducted clustering analyses to verify whether common patterns can be identified from two distinct types of end-stage cancer prognosis discussion information, including patient-centered communication and shared decision making data. We applied hierarchical clustering on patient-centered communication measurement data and frequent itemset hierarchical clustering on coded shared decision-making interaction information. Our results suggested modest association between the two data sets in clustering assignments when measuring it with a normalized mutual information index. However, we could not find any noticeable overlap between the two assignments.
